      "notes": {
        "summary": "Static bodies coming and going no longer stall a step: the tree of them is kept up to date instead of built again from all of them, so streaming a tile of them in or out costs a step some 2 ms, not 30. The tree is turned where that shrinks a box, so it answers as fast after streaming as one built afresh. A ray strikes the same body, triangle and normal whatever order the tree meets them in, and twin worlds built in different orders step alike."
